## Ansible Conventions

### Privilege model
Scripts run as `db2inst1` via Ansible `become`. The sudoers entry must be scoped to
the exact script path:
```
ansible_svc ALL=(db2inst1) NOPASSWD: /home/db2inst1/scripts/online/runstats.sh
```
Claude must not suggest broader sudo grants. If a new script needs execution rights,
a new scoped sudoers line is required — not a wildcard.

### Online playbook pattern
```yaml
- name: Run <script>
  shell: "/home/db2inst1/scripts/online/<script>.sh {{ dbname }} {{ schema }} {{ mode | default('sampled') }}"
  become: true
  become_user: db2inst1
  register: script_result
  ignore_errors: true

- name: Parse JSON summary
  set_fact:
    summary: "{{ script_result.stdout_lines | last | from_json }}"

- name: Trigger downstream play if candidates found
  include_tasks: <downstream>.yml
  vars:
    targets: "{{ summary.<candidate_field> }}"
  when: summary.<candidate_field> | length > 0

- name: Fail play if script errored
  fail:
    msg: "{{ summary }}"
  when: summary.exit_code | int != 0
```

### Offline playbook pattern
Offline playbooks **must** include an AWX approval node before the script execution task.
Claude must include this when generating any offline playbook. Do not omit it.

```yaml
- name: Request maintenance window approval
  awx.awx.workflow_approval:
    name: "Approve offline REORG - {{ dbname }}.{{ schema }}"
    description: "Offline REORG requires DBA and change management sign-off"
    timeout: 3600
```

### Concurrency
AWX job template concurrency limit must be set to 1 per database+schema combination.
If Claude is asked to create a new AWX job template definition, always include:
```yaml
allow_simultaneous: false
```

